menu "Camera Driver"

config JETTYD_CAMERA_SUPPORTED
    bool "Enable camera driver (OV2640)"
    default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    help
        Compile the full OV2640 camera implementation.
        On non-camera targets (esp32c3, esp32c6) this is automatically
        disabled and camera_register() compiles to a no-op stub so all
        CI matrix legs remain green.

config JETTYD_CAMERA_SETTLE_FRAMES
    int "AE/AWB settle frames to discard after sensor init"
    default 5
    range 0 30
    depends on JETTYD_CAMERA_SUPPORTED
    help
        Number of frames to grab and immediately discard right after the
        OV2640 is initialised, before the first frame that gets uploaded.

        The sensor's first frames after power-up are underexposed (the very
        first is typically pitch black); auto-exposure and auto-white-balance
        converge only after several frames. Discarding these settle frames
        ensures a grant-triggered capture never uploads a black/garbage frame.

        Default 5 (matches the ~3-5 frame convergence seen during P4 camera
        bring-up). Set to 0 to disable settling.

endmenu
